  "narrative": {
    "summaryIntro": "Dwarkadhish Temple, located in the ancient city of Dwarka in Gujarat, is one of the four cardinal pilgrimage sites (Char Dham) and is dedicated to Lord Krishna. The temple is believed to be built on the site where Krishna ruled his kingdom and is a major center of Vaishnavite worship. The present structure stands at a height of approximately 51.5 meters with elaborate stone carvings.\n\nAccording to Hindu tradition, Dwarka was the capital of Krishna's kingdom and remains a sacred pilgrimage destination. The temple features intricate architectural details characteristic of Gujarat's temple-building tradition. It is revered as one of the oldest and most important Krishna temples in India, attracting devotees year-round.",
